Package: zutempo
Title: Dates, Times and Durations Following 'JavaScript' Temporal
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Ecma International", role = "cph",
           comment = "Test262 tests translated into tests/testthat/test262/, see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
  )
Description: An implementation of the Temporal date and time model of
    'ECMAScript', the language standard 'ECMA-262' behind 'JavaScript',
    in 'R', with a native 'C' core: 'Instant', 'ZonedDateTime',
    'PlainDateTime', 'PlainDate', 'PlainTime', 'PlainYearMonth',
    'PlainMonthDay', 'Duration' and 'Now', in the ISO 8601 calendar, with
    the time zones of the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) read
    from the same database that base 'R' uses. Values are stored exactly
    in 'R' vectors, arithmetic is done over the specification's full
    ranges with exact 128-bit intermediates, and strings follow the
    Internet Extended Date/Time Format of RFC 9557, with annotations.
    Every result is meant to match the result of the same operation in a
    browser or in 'Node.js'.
